WEBVTT

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:06.150
Why do you ask?

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.430
Fame and riches just come as part of the package.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:11.030
As for me,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:16.600
I just think about how to bat and how to lead before every game I play.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.930
I see.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:24.210
That sounds more like my style.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:27.280
I'll stop meaninglessly over thinking it,

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.510
and just focus on winning this game.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:40.140
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:40.140
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.440
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.440
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.820
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.820
the only thing I truly have

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:56.110
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:56.110
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:01.450
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:01.450
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:06.710
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:06.710
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:12.090
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:12.090
I had begun to understand many things

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:18.180
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:18.180
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.720
garakuta no yama kara

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.720
In the junk I've piled up,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.810
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.810
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:33.110
hibike kono koe yo

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:33.110
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:39.410
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:39.410
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:45.040
namida kareru made

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:45.040
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:50.080
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:50.080
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:55.420
namida hareru made

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:55.420
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:55.420 --> 00:02:00.430
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:55.420 --> 00:02:00.430
though I may lose my way,

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:04.270
egakikake no ima

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:04.270
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.770
kizamu

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:11.520
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.060
akashi

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:11.520
kono te de

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:17.280
Rookies' Troubles

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:17.280
Rookies' Troubles

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.950
The Wings go on the offensive, beginning with their top batter.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:30.580
Shigeno's on the mound, and he's been getting outs even with runners on bases.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.780
Unlike his usual power pitches,

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.880
he's been pitching to contact today, focusing on control and hitting the corners, and giving no runs to the Wings.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.960
No walks yet today either.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:45.320
If he holds down this inning, this game may become his first shutout in the majors.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.980
He's pitching quite well, wouldn't you say, Mr. Shigeno?

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.900
Yes.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.110
Let's go with a forkball here.

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:07.410
Shoot!

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:23.250
Sorry.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.740
I should've caught that.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.600
No, I made a bad throw.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.990
Good work.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:32.100
Watts can take it from here.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.020
Shigeno was doing quite well today,

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.820
but after letting another runner get on base, he'll finish for today.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.600
A double play.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:10.730
Watts pulls through with just two pitches.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.770
His reliability is second to none.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.980
His pitching speed and control are both impressive.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.840
And that's the game.

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:29.120
The Hornets have a shutout with pitching from Shigeno and Watts.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.090
Thanks for taking care of that.

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:32.140
I owe you.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.540
Sure, it's my job.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.390
Are you doing anything after this?

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:44.440
Want to go celebrate with some good food?

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.290
Sounds like a plan.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:49.850
But I have to say, Shigeno did a great job today.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:52.920
That's what I call tough pitching.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.900
Well, it certainly wasn't bad,

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.480
but compared to when he first started...

00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.430
Yeah.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:02.410
His pitching was so much more intense.

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.690
Mr. Shigeno, may I have a moment?

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:06.950
Yeah?

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.670
You have a visitor.

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:09.610
A visitor?

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:12.710
Intense, huh...

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:18.620
You really can't feel his intensity anymore.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:23.620
When he was with the Bats, he was full of spirit,

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:27.660
and his desire to win was off the charts.

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:31.170
Yet now...

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.270
He's changed, you know.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.950
A visitor?

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:40.270
Who could it possibly be?

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:45.060
Yo.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.110
It's been a while.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.410
Dad?!

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:56.040
The day game between the Texas Raiders and the Arizona Eagles

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:01.320
led to an astounding chance for the Raiders in the ninth inning.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.820
Gibson Jr. was at bat, batting seventh.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:07.580
He hasn't been doing well lately, but will he turn the game around,

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:10.120
or be the last batter?

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.010
Here's the first pitch.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:18.000
Not surprisingly, Gibson Jr. hits an easy fly for the catcher.

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:21.740
That was the seventh straight loss for the Raiders,

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:23.490
putting them last in the central division.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:29.530
Gibson Jr. was batting seventh today, but he's fallen into a slump, failing on two great chances.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:35.470
He was a golden rookie as the top draft pick, but his second year has been harsh.

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:39.890
That was a terrible play.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.530
Man, I can't believe myself.

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:45.720
Junior.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:48.110
What are you doing here?

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:52.140
You saw my game today, right?

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:55.390
The manager called me in after.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:00.600
You were in good shape in the exhibition games and early in the season,

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:06.320
but your average has been falling since May and you haven't had a single home run.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.770
Your average is .250.

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:12.490
What's going on with you?

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:15.680
I don't know.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:20.080
I've been working on my batting with the coach.

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:24.850
Well, people have more data on you in the second year, and you're still young.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:28.160
We don't expect everything to go perfectly in the majors.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:32.300
I'm sure you're just tired from playing non-stop since the World Cup.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.530
We're taking you off the starting line-up for the Bisons game in two days.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.590
You need a break.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.770
Pathetic.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:49.230
The season is just starting, and I'm already off the line-up.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:51.060
I see.

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:54.030
But you can't blame them after your poor performances.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:58.290
Please help me, Dad.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.580
I don't know what I'm doing wrong.

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:06.920
I've played baseball all my life, but I've never had this happen.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:11.170
You came here from Arizona for something that stupid?

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.840
Stupid?

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.700
I'm a pitcher.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.660
How should I know anything about batters?

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:22.960
How about using a tennis racket?

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.190
Maybe it'd be easier to hit.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:28.050
Though I don't know if it'd go very far.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.280
Don't give me that!

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:35.310
I come all this way to ask for help, and this is how you treat me?

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:40.000
I was hoping you could give me some advice since you've always watched over me.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.200
You call yourself a parent?!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.310
Give me a break.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:52.880
I guess you wouldn't know how it feels to be in a slump considering your stability in the majors.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:58.910
Damn it.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.340
Hey, Junior.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.050
A slump?

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:11.030
Know your place, rookie.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:16.200
You need years of success in the majors to go into a slump.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.030
Go back to the minors?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.150
Sure, why not?

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:28.290
It takes suffering and frustration to become a top major leaguer.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:32.280
You came to me because you were taken off the line-up?

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.460
Don't be a baby!

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:38.600
Yeah, all right!

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.820
I'll never come to you again!

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.780
Was that okay?

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:57.030
He finally started to visit again.

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.970
If you push him away now...

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.950
It's fine, Emma.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:11.290
Geez, you should've told me that you were coming.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.720
I almost pissed myself when I saw you.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.800
Not to mention, you've been commentating for the games.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.090
What are you saying?

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:21.710
I heard you hung up on Mom when she tried to tell you.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:23.180
Really?

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.400
Geez, this knife is a piece of junk.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.720
Are you a dog or something?

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.140
Where are your manners?

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:35.070
Blame the knife.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.660
By the way, Dad...

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:43.540
Yeah, what is it?

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:49.470
If you're not going to eat that, can I have it?

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:50.370
O-Oh, sure.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.940
Thanks.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:10:59.200
Man, that was some good grub.

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.760
Thanks, Dad.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.510
Don't give me that.

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:05.060
You're in the majors, so stop freeloading off your dad.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.620
Well, I'm going back to the hotel.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:10.480
Good luck on your next game.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:12.990
Hey, Dad.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:16.420
You saw my pitching today.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:17.320
How was it?

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:23.460
You paid attention to the corners and pitched to contact.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:26.240
Your pitching looked mature.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.710
Right?

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:30.960
It took a lot of effort to get here.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.460
I got demoted once, but I'm over it now.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.470
Hey, Goro.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:42.550
Now that you've become a professional, you're not just pitching for yourself anymore.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.350
Don't ever forget that.

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:48.480
See ya.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:50.590
Make sure you call Mom from time to time.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:19.550
Strike out!

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:20.340
Game over.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:23.170
That's the third straight win for the Hornets.

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.270
The interleague matches began today.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:30.310
The Hornets have started them off with a win.

00:12:30.900 --> 00:12:34.380
Watts did a great job closing again.

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:37.680
This is Shigeno's third win as well.

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:40.700
Yes, he gave up three runs in six innings,

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:42.240
but the batters helped him out.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.510
Shigeno has a 3-3 record this season.

00:12:45.510 --> 00:12:48.950
He seems to be recovering, with two of those wins coming after he returned.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.620
I must say, that was a good game.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.180
Three straight wins and our win-loss ratio is fifty percent.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:01.250
Considering we're only three wins away from the top, we're still in good shape.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:05.200
Shigeno's recovered, and Keene's a batting champion.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:09.180
Having healthy youngsters keeps the team alive.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:14.100
Shigeno, you're looking completely different with your calm pitching.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:18.020
You used to break down after letting a runner on base,

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:25.240
but you only walked two batters today and kept your pitches low with three double plays.

00:13:25.910 --> 00:13:28.420
You're pretty good for your age.

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:30.280
It's as if you're a veteran pitcher.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:35.810
Oh yeah, Shigeno.

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:39.440
Your next game's against the Raiders in a week, right?

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:41.130
Oh, yeah.

00:13:41.650 --> 00:13:46.690
It'd be a perfect chance to pay Gibson Jr. back for the World Cup,

00:13:46.690 --> 00:13:50.220
but I hear he's in a slump and isn't on the line-up anymore.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:53.280
He isn't on the line-up?

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.450
Junior isn't?

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:56.490
What, you didn't know?

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:57.700
No.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:02.110
I saw the stats from their game, and it looked like he was back on the starting line-up today.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:06.640
He got three hits, so maybe he's out of his slump.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:14.620
In the bottom of the seventh, the Raiders have runners on second and third with just one out.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:18.870
Gibson Jr. is back on the starting line-up today.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:21.380
It's through!

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.460
It's a hit!

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:25.470
Both runners come in to score, and the Raiders now lead 7-1.

00:14:25.470 --> 00:14:29.550
Gibson Jr. seems to be out of his slump with those two RBIs.

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:39.830
Can I have your signature?

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.270
Can I shake your hand?

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:45.750
Thank you.

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.250
Thank you very much.

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:50.570
U-Um...

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:56.290
C-Can you sign my ball?

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:57.550
Sure.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:04.130
Here.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.100
Thank you!

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:06.990
See ya.

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:13.470
I'll be cheering for you in your next game!

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.370
Good luck!

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:23.800
The Hornets' pitcher facing the Raiders line-up today will be...

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:26.440
Goro Shigeno!

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:31.220
It's his first face-off with Junior since the World Cup.

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:31.890
Yeah.

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:33.410
I'm looking forward to it.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.490
Shigeno! Shigeno!

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:35.490
Shigeno! Shigeno!

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:36.640
Good luck!

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:41.980
The crowd is going wild and the game hasn't even started.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:45.710
I bet they're all looking forward to your match with Gibson Jr.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:48.130
Like I care about that.

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.870
Junior's just another batter.

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:56.050
My mind's only set on getting them out one by one.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:04.810
Now hitting, number 3: Schweitzer!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.590
Play ball!

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:15.380
Strike!

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.080
Out!

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:25.760
Now hitting, number 9: Mathis!

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:30.610
Strike!

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:34.510
He's pitching well today too.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:39.270
Looks like we won't be busy until about the fifth inning.

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:40.450
We'll see about that.

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:44.690
The Raiders have a pretty strong line-up.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:48.110
It won't be as easy as his previous two games.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:48.730
What?

00:16:55.130 --> 00:17:00.330
Now hitting, number 4: Joe Gibson Jr!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:04.040
I'm sure you're aware, Sanders.

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:07.330
He may have recovered from the yips,

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:12.050
but his aggression is completely gone.

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:18.140
He's still young, so why doesn't he throw like that anymore?

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:23.160
I sure hope this match with Junior will bring back his old self.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:25.310
Play!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.170
Ball.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:40.660
He's been control pitching ever since he came back up.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:45.910
I would have preferred to have another face-off like at the World Cup, but...

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.470
Ball!

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:55.260
Neither you nor I are in the condition to have a match like that.

00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:58.010
Strike!

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:01.930
It's not easy to survive in the majors.

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:07.690
I have to get a hit no matter what and leave a good record every game.

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.030
Foul!

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:16.110
This is good.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:20.600
If I keep my pitches low, I won't take any serious damage.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:24.090
In order to do well in the majors,

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:29.580
I need to pitch with composure like an adult and keep the game moving!

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:34.550
Out!

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:36.670
Out!

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:38.360
Double play!

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:42.600
Gibson Jr. hits the ball to the shortstop for a double play, and that's three outs.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:46.270
Shigeno pitched through the danger smoothly.

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:50.720
The first round of their rematch went to Shigeno.

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:53.520
Yes, it did.

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:57.710
If it was a little off, it would've been a hit.

00:18:58.420 --> 00:19:01.300
My God. What a weak match.

00:19:01.690 --> 00:19:05.580
Junior's not going to stir up Shigeno like that.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:37.730
You suddenly broke down in the fifth inning.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:41.200
It looked like you were pitching well to contact until then.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.980
What happened?

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:53.710
Well, it happens.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:56.620
I just need to switch gears and win next time.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:04.180
Man, I'm getting tired of his attitude.

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:05.720
Watts.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:09.690
He's been knocked out by the Titans and now the Raiders.

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:14.880
As I thought, he's not effective against strong teams.

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:18.530
With just control pitching,

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:23.660
good batters will work around it and hit with compact swings to the right and the center.

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:28.270
In his state, he'll only be effective against batters with bad swings.

00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:36.960
Hello?

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:38.200
Hey, Shigeno?

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:39.950
It's me, Oliver.

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:43.270
You seem to be doing well.

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:48.850
I was worried your yips might come back against Gibson Jr. today,

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:51.310
but you stayed calm until the end.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:52.420
Yeah.

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:56.690
But I completely fell apart after those two singles.

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:02.280
Have you found a new goal?

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:03.830
No.

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:06.280
I decided not to worry about it.

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:12.090
I just think about doing the best I can in every game.

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:16.030
Baseball's how I live.

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:18.880
That in itself is like my goal now.

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:20.170
I see.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:22.650
And I have more.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.090
About a week ago,

00:21:25.620 --> 00:21:27.840
Mr. Gibson gave me a call.

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:30.930
G-Gibson?

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.310
Yeah.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:35.540
He heard that I was helping you with your yips,

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:39.230
and he asked about your condition and how well the recovery went.

00:22:01.260 --> 00:22:02.670
You're starting tomorrow, right?

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:04.130
I'll catch your pitches later.

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:06.340
Oh, thanks.

00:22:06.340 --> 00:22:07.430
Hey, Shigeno!

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:08.840
I've got news!

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:10.430
What's wrong?

00:22:10.430 --> 00:22:11.560
Why are you in a rush?

00:22:11.560 --> 00:22:14.100
"What's wrong?"

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:15.790
A-An emergency press conference!

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:17.080
A conference?

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:18.020
For what?

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:21.810
Gibson is coming out of retirement and is back on the Bisons!

00:22:25.690 --> 00:22:27.280
Basically,

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:29.780
he's back to play!

00:22:33.020 --> 00:22:35.870
Wh-What?

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:59.480
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:59.480
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:04.770
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:04.770
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:11.030
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:11.030
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:15.830
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:15.830
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:22.500
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:22.500
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:28.300
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:28.300
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:34.100
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:34.100
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:39.560
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:39.560
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:46.020
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:46.020
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:51.280
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:54.700
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:54.700
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:57.200
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.700 --> 00:24:03.580
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:03.580
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:07.420
sotto

00:24:03.670 --> 00:24:07.420
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:15.600
Preview

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:15.600
Preview

00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:14.220
Gibson is back in the majors?

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:17.680
And he's going to pitch in the same game as me?

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:20.890
What the hell is that old man thinking?

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:25.270
Next time, on Major: An Electrifying Return.

00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:27.650
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:29.770
Next Time

00:24:25.270 --> 00:24:29.770
Next Time

